course: dictionary
lesson: 15728
title: Transcription: a written copy
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A transcription is a written copy of words that were first spoken, recorded or written somewhere else. Look for clues around the word. «The teacher made a transcription of the class interview so we could read what everyone said.» The word «interview» and the phrase «so we could read» tell you that a transcription is words written down from speech.
explain: Transcription can also mean the act of writing something down. «Sam spent the evening doing the transcription of his grandad's stories.» Here it is the job of writing the stories out, not the written copy itself. Ask yourself: is the sentence about the copy, or about the writing? The clue tells you which.
explain: In a dictionary, a phonetic transcription shows how a word sounds, using special symbols. «The dictionary gave a phonetic transcription of the word, so I knew how to say it.» The clue is «how to say it», so phonetic transcription must be about sounds.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and each meaning needs its own clues. In music, a transcription is a piece rewritten for different instruments. In biology, transcription is the copying of information from DNA in a cell. When you meet transcription, read the words around it first, then check your meaning fits the sentence.
fact: A transcription is a written copy of speech, a recording, or a text.
fact: «Transcription» can also mean the act of writing down speech or copying a text.
fact: A phonetic transcription uses special symbols to show how a word sounds, as in a dictionary.
fact: In music, a transcription is a piece rewritten so different instruments can play it.
fact: In biology, transcription is the copying of information from DNA in a cell.
exercise: «The teacher made a transcription of the class interview we recorded.» What is a transcription here? | A song sung loudly by the class | A drawing of the teacher | A video of the classroom | *A written copy of the words that were spoken
exercise: «The dictionary gives a phonetic transcription of each word.» What does a phonetic transcription show? | The history of the word in old books | The number of letters in the word | *How the word sounds, written with special symbols | A picture of the word
exercise: «The school band played a transcription of a piano piece.» What does transcription mean in music? | *A piece rewritten for different instruments | A song with no words | A piece played in a different room | A piece with no notes at all
test: «Sam's job is to make a transcription of every speech at the school assembly.» What does transcription mean here? | A song sung at assembly | A loud speaker | A painting of the hall | *The act of writing down the speech
test: «In biology, transcription is the copying of information from DNA in a cell.» What is copied during transcription? | Water from the cell | The cell's walls and colour | A picture of the cell | *Information from DNA
exam: «Historians made a transcription of the old letters so everyone could read the handwriting.» What did the historians do? | They painted pictures of the letters | They burned the old letters | They sold the letters to a museum | *They wrote out the letters as a readable copy
